bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.6-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Terrain test pass v0.4.5 fixes (2 reproducible bugs across 14 audits
    on 6 distinct systems, including production hardware).
  * Bug 1: bob/checks/kernel_modules.py — dpkg-query did not filter on
    'ii' state, so kernels left in 'rc' state after `apt remove` (without
    --purge) were still listed as installed. Now uses
    ${db:Status-Abbrev}|${Package} and keeps only lines whose 2nd char
    is 'i' (covers 'ii' and 'hi'; excludes 'rc', 'pn', 'un', 'iU').
  * Bug 2: bob/domain_scores.py::active_domains_from_engine() — scoring
    inversion after remediation. The actionable filter widened from
    (WARN, ALERT) to (OK, WARN, ALERT), so a domain that goes clean
    (only `updates.ok` left) stays at 10/10 in the global average
    instead of disappearing from the denominator. INFO-only domains
    remain hidden by design.
  * 4500 tests (+11 vs v0.4.5).
  * Multi-distro integration CI (additive): GitHub Actions matrix runs
    BOB inside containers of Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/25.04,
    Kali Rolling, Fedora 41 on every push/PR to main.

 -- Cédric Clauzel <cedricclauzel@mailo.com>  Sun, 17 May 2026 17:45:45 +0200

bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.5-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Test infrastructure hardening release (pure refactor of
    tests/test_locale_coverage.py — no source file in bob/ modified).
  * Switched the locale-coverage scanner from regex over Python source
    to ast.parse + ast.walk. Eliminates three classes of regex false
    positive: docstring matches, multi-line call site fragility, and
    obj._t(...) attribute calls. The _KEY_EXCLUSIONS allowlist that
    was the symptom of the regex limitation is deleted.
  * Same external contract: 9 tests in TestLocaleCoverage +
    TestExplainNamespaceCoverage + TestPlaceholderParity.
  * 4489 tests (unchanged total vs v0.4.4).

 -- Cédric Clauzel <cedricclauzel@mailo.com>  Sun, 17 May 2026 09:00:39 +0200

bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.4-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=high

  * Cross-distro terrain hardening release. One critical bug + three
    minor presentation fixes surfaced by terrain testing on Debian 13,
    Kali Rolling, Mint test, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.
  * Critical: bob/checks/updates.py reported "system up to date" on
    100% of vierge Debian-family VMs (Debian 13 with 59 packages
    pending, Kali Rolling with 868, Mint with 33, Ubuntu LTS with 23
    of which 21 were security updates) because (a) `apt-get -s upgrade`
    is conservative and back-holds anything pulling a new package
    (typical kernel), (b) stale apt cache silently returned 0 packages.
    Now uses `apt-get -s dist-upgrade`, detects stale cache (mtime >
    7 days), cross-checks via `apt list --upgradable`, and propagates
    `updates_unknown` to the "Surface d'attaque" section instead of
    the false "up to date".
  * Minor: AppArmor "0 profiles loaded" dedicated key (was confusing
    on Kali); SMART check skipped when all disks are virtual; DDNS
    ports inlined in the WARN message.
  * Picked up the v0.4.3 audit-deferred items (S4 home-bounded
    symlink, M4 _parse_ufw_covered_ports refactor, I2 wave-2 key= on
    services and virtualization, locale-coverage test).
  * 4489 tests (+21 vs v0.4.3).

 -- Cédric Clauzel <cedricclauzel@mailo.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 07:50:21 +0200

bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Doc catch-up + post-audit hardening pass.
  * 4 firewall explanation keys promoted to EXPLAIN_KEYS (frozen API
    contract). Short CHANGELOG corrected for v0.4.2.
  * Critical: --json --json-full crashed on HardeningSnapshot because
    of 5 dead attribute references (kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled,
    kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone, fs.protected_fifos,
    fs.protected_regular, kernel.modules_disabled).
  * Important: strptime("%b ...") made locale-independent (broke when
    LANG=fr_FR set the C library to French month names) in ssl_certs
    and logs.
  * Important: _is_covered_by_ufw IP false-positive killed
    (192.168.1.22 matched as covering port 22).
  * Important: cron range validator now rejects out-of-bounds values.
  * Important: email body Markdown links no longer escaped to HTML.
  * key= attribute added to ~30 findings (docker, firewall_stack,
    network_context, ports). 7 dead locale keys removed. i18n concat
    anti-pattern resolved in ddns and logs.
  * 4468 tests (+16).

